      "The best fence stain for most homeowners. A true penetrating oil that soaks into the wood instead of sitting on top, so it wears gracefully instead of peeling.",
    description:
      "Ready Seal has built a devoted following among fence and deck installers, and after a full year of testing on a pressure-treated pine privacy fence, it's easy to see why. This is a genuine penetrating oil stain, meaning the linseed and mineral oil blend soaks into the wood fibers rather than sitting on the surface as a film. That distinction matters enormously for long-term performance: film-forming stains eventually crack and peel because the surface layer can't flex with the wood as it expands and contracts through seasonal humidity swings. Ready Seal never has that problem because there's no film to fail. During our test, we applied a single coat with a pump sprayer and back-rolled it into the grain — the entire 120-linear-foot fence took under two hours, with zero backbrushing required. That's the other reason contractors love this product: unlike most oil stains, Ready Seal doesn't need to be worked into the wood or tipped off to avoid lap marks. Overlaps and heavy spots simply even out on their own as the oil migrates into the grain over the following 24 hours. Twelve months later, water still beaded up on the treated boards rather than soaking in, and the color had faded only slightly on the harshest south-facing sections. The semi-transparent formula lets you see the wood's natural grain and knots while adding a warm amber-brown tone (also available in cedar, redwood, and dark walnut tones). Coverage runs 150-200 square feet per gallon on smooth pine and closer to 100-125 on rough-sawn cedar, which soaks up more product. Dry-to-touch time is about 8 hours, with full cure in 3-5 days depending on humidity. Reapplication is needed every 2-3 years on fences facing full sun, longer in shaded yards. The main tradeoff is smell — plan to stain on a day when you can keep pets and kids away from the fence line for the first 24 hours.",
  },
  {
    id: "behr-premium-solid",
    name: "Behr Premium Solid Color Waterproofing Stain",
    category: "Water-Based Solid Color Stain",
    badge: "Best Solid Color",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B00L21Y9BM?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=osi&th=1&psc=1",
    rating: 4.4,
    reviewCount: 14800,
    pros: [
      "Opaque solid color completely hides old stain, discoloration, and repairs",
      "Widely available in thousands of custom tint colors at Home Depot",
      "Water-based formula cleans up with soap and water, low odor",
      "Excellent UV blocking — pigment load resists fading better than transparent stains",
      "Backed by Behr's satisfaction guarantee and easy in-store color matching",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Fully hides the wood grain — not a look everyone wants on a nicer fence",
      "Solid stains show wear at high-traffic contact points (gate latches, post tops)",
